cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus in research or publication, please cite as below."
title: "Trithemius Corpus: machine-assisted English translations of a 47-work Latin corpus by Johannes Trithemius"
abstract: >
  A machine-assisted English translation of a 47-work Latin corpus by Johannes
  Trithemius (Benedictine abbot of Sponheim, 1462-1516), produced via a
  retrieval-augmented LLM translation pipeline, re-OCR, independent grading,
  targeted remediation, and keep-better revision. The current public release
  covers 4,400 published chunks across 47 translatable printed editions
  (29 distinct texts), with 4,353 graded chunks, a chunk-weighted mean
  faithfulness of 4.63/5, 0.0% confirmed hallucination, and an all-S public
  tier distribution (S=47 / A=0 / B=0 / C=0 / F=0). The corpus covers
  Trithemius's monastic, devotional, hagiographic, bibliographic, and
  cryptographic writings, including 23 of its 29 distinct texts (39 of
  47 editions) with no located prior published English translation.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Fabin
    given-names: Ian Carlos
    alias: Carlosian
    website: "https://github.com/agentcarlosian"
keywords:
  - Trithemius
  - Latin
  - English translation
  - digital humanities
  - LLM translation
  - early modern
  - monastic literature
  - cryptography
  - Renaissance
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Trithemius-Corpus/Trithemius-Corpus"
url: "https://trithemius-corpus.github.io/Trithemius-Corpus/"
date-released: 2026-07-12
references:
  - type: book
    authors:
      - family-names: Behrendt
        given-names: Roland
    title: "In Praise of Scribes: De Laude Scriptorum"
    year: 1974
    publisher:
      name: Coronado Press
    location: Lawrence, Kansas
    notes: >
      Prior published English translation of De Laude Scriptorum Manualium
      (manifest entry prdl-24362). The present corpus's rendering of that work
      is an independent machine-assisted translation; users seeking a scholarly
      English edition of that single work should prefer Behrendt's translation.
  - type: book
    authors:
      - family-names: Bongie
        given-names: Elizabeth
    title: "In Praise of Scribes (De Laude Scriptorum)"
    year: 1977
    publisher:
      name: Alcuin Society
    location: Vancouver
    notes: >
      A second prior published English translation of De Laude Scriptorum
      Manualium (prdl-24362), alongside Behrendt 1974.
  - type: generic
    authors:
      - family-names: Lilly
        given-names: William
    title: "The World's Catastrophe"
    year: 1647
    notes: >
      Early English version/adaptation of Trithemius's De Septem Secundeis
      (manifest entry prdl-24383).
  - type: generic
    authors:
      - family-names: Neal
        given-names: Philip
    title: "Partial English translation of the preface to Trithemius's Polygraphia"
    notes: >
      The only located prior English of any part of the Polygraphia
      (prdl-24389/prdl-24390/prdl-24391); covers the prefatory matter only.
      This corpus supplies the first located continuous English of the body.
  - type: book
    authors:
      - family-names: Skinner
        given-names: Stephen
      - family-names: Clark
        given-names: Daniel
    title: "Steganographia: Books I-IV"
    year: 2024
    publisher:
      name: Llewellyn
    notes: >
      Comprehensive modern English edition of Trithemius's Steganographia.
      The clavis works in this corpus (prdl-70281, prdl-70282) cover different
      source editions but treat overlapping subject matter.
